body:
Surely you can't search for foo and bar in the same interface? the query must be equal if you're going to do a single UI.

However what you can do is map the fields to be the same across all record types:

```
// before
{ a: 'something' }, { b: 'something' }
// after
{ a: 'something', combined: 'something' }, { b: 'something', combined: 'something' }
```

You can still use a or b conditionally to display record-specific information, as long as the actual searchable attributes are equal, you can rank them.

In a lot of cases you can even use the first records, and simply add both a and b in the searchable attributes.

If I'm missing something, please give real examples of records that should and shouldn't match different queries.
